gs memoryview() and bytes() ask a __buffer__ for."] [365 1 "// bufferOf is a class's __buffer__(flags): its memoryview, nil when the type has none (PY7: memoryview() and bytes()"] [366 1 "// of such an object raised TypeError)."] [387 1 "// ExtBufferHook is the buffer of an object whose type a C extension made with bf_getbuffer (arbace/pyctypes, queue"] [388 1 "// 270b): its view (found false when the type has none), as bufferOf's of a class's __buffer__."] [391 1 "// NewBytesView is a memoryview of the bytes b (format 'B'), read-only when readonly, for ExtBufferHook's views."] [396 1 "// releaseBuffer is PyBuffer_Release of a view bufferOf got: the exporter's __release_buffer__(view), when it has one."] [405 1 "// release is memoryview.release(): the exporter's buffer released once."] [427 1 "// mvItemSizes are get_native_fmtchar's formats and their native sizes (64-bit Linux; queue 263: n N f d e ? P too)."] [431 1 "// mvFmtChar is a native single-character format without its optional '@' (get_native_fmtchar's character)."] [439 1 "// mvFmtSize is get_native_fmtchar: a native format's item size, false when f is none (3.15.2: also \"Zf\" and \"Zd\","] [440 1 "// the complex formats; 3.14.10: one character only)."] [455 1 "// mvByteFmt is IS_BYTE_FORMAT of a view's format: 'b', 'B' or 'c', with an optional '@'."] [472 1 "// item is the i-th item of a cast view: little-endian, signed for the lower-case formats."] [477 54 "// queue 263: unpack_single's other native formats, as the struct module's"] [478 31 "// 3.15.2's complexes: the struct module's F and D, native"] [519 1 "// BytesLike makes a memoryview a bytes-like object (asBytes): a copy of its bytes."] [533 4 "// a view of a view: the same buffer, start, length and stride (CPython's memory_from_buffer keeps the"] [534 4 "// strides, so a non-contiguous view stays one)"] [541 42 "// picklebuf_getbuf: the object's own buffer"] [555 4 "// the export of a class's __buffer__: its __release_buffer__ called when the l